# Path: the stages ahead, to the hardware's speed. Each stage names the evidence that closes it.

n: 7.2
name: stage-1-answers-and-encoding
kind: plan
is: The node encoding is fixed in writing (5.13): canonical bytes, the content id, the canonical print and the catalogue, with 127 conformance vectors, 81 of them malformed. Stage 1 closes when a second hand has implemented a reader from the page alone and the vectors hold in it; that has not been done.
status: inferred
from: 5.13 6.1.1 6.1.3 6.1.8 5.2.2 5.3.4 5.1.5 5.11.4
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.3
name: stage-2-floor
kind: plan
is: The C bootstrap under its budget: the framebuffer, store, canonical reader, walker, page birth and host table. It stands (5.14.10): the ground programs run, a frozen node thaws to the same id, a machine-code leaf runs both unsigned and under the hardened runtime, the build fails over its line count, and a second process records a live run and replays it. It closes when the host functions for symbol lookup, the framework trampoline, threads and the clock are written (5.14.9).
status: inferred
from: 5.9.1 5.9.2 5.9.3 5.9.4 5.11.4 5.7.6
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.4
name: stage-3-home-lens
kind: plan
is: The home lens as rows written in the grammar, read forwards and printed backwards. Closes when the lens reads its own definition, prints it, and the reprint reads to the same nodes.
status: inferred
from: 5.3.2 5.3.5 5.3.3
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.5
name: stage-4-self-compile
kind: plan
is: The one-pass emitter written in the grammar compiles the compiler. Closes when the system regenerates its own seed byte for byte, cold and compiled runs print the same values over the whole core, and the walker is off the running path after the cold start.
status: inferred
from: 5.10.4 5.10.1 5.10.8 5.9.5 5.10.5
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.6
name: stage-5-control-and-objects
kind: plan
is: Choice with commit, the trail, declared reversibility, the reference pair, composed parents and templates. Closes when the thesis example of a class with two parents runs as one composed shape with the view moving on a super-send, a failed option's effects are undone, and each of those tests has been turned red by a planted fault.
status: inferred
from: 5.4.6 5.4.7 5.4.8 5.4.9 5.5.1 5.5.2 5.5.5 5.11.1
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.7
name: stage-6-speed
kind: plan
is: The optimizing tier, then matrix instructions, then the GPU backend. Closes on measurements against optimized C for the same kernels on this machine, with lines of meaning and lines of speed reported apart.
status: inferred
from: 5.10.6 5.10.7 5.10.10
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.8
name: stage-7-lenses
kind: plan
is: A first host-language lens, Go, since NUMS.Go mapped it; then a second; then the first human-language lens. Closes when one program read through two host lenses yields nodes whose shared and differing blueprints are both shown, and the lens declines by name what it cannot print.
status: inferred
from: 5.3.6 5.3.7 6.1.19
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.9
name: stage-8-self-replacement
kind: plan
is: The system writes its own signed executable image and starts from it. Closes when every piece of the C file has a compiled counterpart running in its place and the C file is needed only for a cold start on a new host.
status: inferred
from: 5.9.6 5.9.7
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.10
name: flows-first
kind: decision
is: The owner's direction of 2026-11-25: doors, gates, receipts and bands were a distraction in the old body. The work here follows end-to-end flows that really run, observed in real time through shared memory and the framebuffer of 5.7.6.
status: given
by: owner
see: 5.7.6
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.11
name: built-with-a-c-compiler-alone
kind: decision
is: The owner's direction of 2026-11-25: this is a new repository, and the old kernel and its runtime are not used to build it. Everything here builds with a C compiler and make. The old body appears only as evidence that was read (hubs 2 and 3), never as a tool, a dependency or a step of any build or check.
status: given
by: owner
see: 5.9.1 2.1
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.12
name: each-stage-closes-on-a-watched-run
kind: plan
is: From stage 3 on, a stage closes on a real run of the thing it adds, recorded from a second process through the framebuffer and replayed, in addition to the evidence its own node names. 'make watch' is the first such run.
status: inferred
from: 7.10 5.7.6 5.11.3
at: 2026-11-25
